    <item>
      <title>2024 Underwater Rover</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/projects/rov/2024/2024/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 01 Sep 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><author>tedi.qafko@gmail.com (Tedi Qafko)</author>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/projects/rov/2024/2024/</guid>
      <description>&lt;link rel=&#34;stylesheet&#34; href=&#34;http://localhost:1313/css/custom.css&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;style&gt;&#xA;    .power-container {&#xA;        display: flex;&#xA;        flex-wrap: wrap;&#xA;        gap: 20px;&#xA;        align-items: center;&#xA;    }&#xA;&#xA;    .power-image {&#xA;        flex: 1;&#xA;        text-align: center;&#xA;    }&#xA;&#xA;    .power-image img {&#xA;        max-width: 100%;&#xA;        height: auto;&#xA;        border-radius: 8px;&#xA;    }&#xA;&#xA;    .power-text {&#xA;        flex: 1;&#xA;    }&#xA;&#xA;    @media (max-width: 768px) { .power-container { flex-direction: column; text-align: left; }&#xA;                                .power-image img { width: 100%; }&#xA;    }&#xA;    @media (max-width: 768px){ div[style*=&#34;display:flex&#34;] &gt; div { flex-basis: 100% !important; }}&#xA;&lt;/style&gt;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;overview&#34;&gt;Overview&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Designed a Remotely Operated Vehicle equipped with cameras, sonar, and environmental sensors for underwater exploration. The system features onboard computing for navigation, data analysis, and communication, along with electric thrusters and robotic arms for movement, object manipulation, and sample collection.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Object Tracking Sphere</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/projects/object-tracking-sphere/sphere/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 05 Mar 2019 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><author>tedi.qafko@gmail.com (Tedi Qafko)</author>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/projects/object-tracking-sphere/sphere/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;overview&#34;&gt;Overview&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A spherical autonomous robot designed for low-cost freshwater monitoring, integrating reaction-wheel actuation, a buoyancy engine, and a modular sensor suite for real-time environmental data collection.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div style=&#34;display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center;&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;video &#xA;    width=&#34;100%&#34; &#xA;    autoplay &#xA;    loop &#xA;    muted &#xA;    playsinline &#xA;    style=&#34;max-width: 100%; width: 100%;&#34;&#xA;  &gt;&#xA;    &lt;source src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/img/sphere/reaction-wheel1.mp4&#34; type=&#34;video/mp4&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/video&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Figure 1.&lt;/strong&gt; A prototype assembly of one of the components in the robot called a reaction wheel. Uses angular momentum to orient the sphere. Two of these on the sphere control 3 degrees of freedom&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
